# The .transaction.lock files are NOT residue and must never be deleted:
# global_market_writer_claim.py serialises every claim mutation on one
# persistent lock inode, and the lock's identity is that inode. Removing it
# while another process holds the descriptor open would let a second process
# create a fresh inode and take a lock that excludes nobody.
#
# Volatile run-gate state: rewritten or appended on every five-minute
# scheduler tick. Launch records and archived writer claims are evidence and
# stay tracked, as do the momentum state and attempts files, which the
# repository committed deliberately in "Record listing momentum automation
# fire". Named individually rather than by wildcard so that decision holds.
docs/agent-log/*.transaction.lock
docs/agent-log/run-gates/*.transaction.lock
docs/agent-log/run-gates/*.claim.json.mutex
docs/agent-log/run-gates/preipo_perpetual_event_automation_state.json
docs/agent-log/run-gates/premarket_perp_listing_automation_state.json
docs/agent-log/run-gates/preipo_perpetual_event_automation_attempts.jsonl
docs/agent-log/run-gates/premarket_perp_listing_automation_attempts.jsonl
docs/agent-log/run-gates/listing_strategy_due_coordinator_state.json
docs/agent-log/run-gates/listing_strategy_due_coordinator_attempts.jsonl
